# Correcting Bodily Circumference Measurments

After height and weight, circumference is the next most readily available metric we can use to assess stature.
The main issue with circumference is that on its own it cannot be easily compared between people.

## Correcting For Height

for the circumference of a specific body part: c<sub>i</sub> it can be corrected by simply dividing by Height.

$$ \frac{c_i^2}{H} $$

This allows different people to compare measurements and hopefully create a more solid basis to research health risks.

